The refactor is complete, compiles cleanly, and is verified behavior-preserving. `Simulator` now has **zero** `instanceof` (and no `(Organism)` cast).

## What changed

The lone `instanceof Organism` in `simulateOneStep` (plus the coupled `(Organism) actor` cast in `generateDisease`) drove two distinct concerns. I promoted both to the `Actor` interface as polymorphic operations.

### Two operations promoted to `Actor`
```java
// disease lifecycle — default: not susceptible
default void exposeToDiseases(List<Disease> diseases, Random rand) { }

// simulation lifecycle — default: act on the live population
default List<Actor> stepTarget(List<Actor> population, List<Actor> nursery) {
